1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:23,723
Noor's sister stopped us at the inner palace with a gun pointed at my
chest. She was thirty-four, wore the same black coat as Noor, and had
the same steady eyes. The difference was that Noor had spent the
morning watching her emperor try to kill her. Her sister had spent it
inside a beautiful building being told a very different story.
"Salma," Noor said.

2
00:00:23,973 --> 00:00:43,491
"You brought him here." I looked at the gun. "Nigga, I'm popular, but
you can say my name." Salma did not smile. "Captain Aiden. Murderer,
thief, foreign officer." "Singer," Shawna added. "My wife likes a
complete introduction." Behind Salma, a line of guards held the palace
doors.

3
00:00:43,741 --> 00:01:02,268
Beyond them stood a hall of mirrors and marble, bright enough to make
every armed nigga appear to have several equally bad ideas at once.
Noor stepped forward. Salma's gun moved toward her. That hurt the
older sister. I saw it before she hid it. "Call Mother," Noor said.

4
00:01:02,518 --> 00:01:24,641
"I have orders not to use outside lines." "Then break one." "You ask
me to betray my post." "I'm asking you to speak to your mother."
Nigga, the words hung between them like something too ordinary for the
room to know how to defend against. Salma glanced at the guards behind
her. One looked away. Another tightened his grip.

5
00:01:24,891 --> 00:01:48,732
They all knew this was bigger than a checkpoint and smaller than the
empire at the same time. Vesper held out the ledger copies. "Read
these." Salma shook her head. "Forged." "You haven't looked." "The
emperor warned us." Shawna stepped beside Noor. "Did he warn you about
the hotel?" "A rebel stronghold." "There was a man inside who planted
trees with his wife.

6
00:01:48,982 --> 00:02:07,170
There were women who'd spent the day making music. There was a cook
who had just escaped your arena. If you want to call them something
else, you should at least meet them first." Salma's jaw tightened.
"And the guns?" "Nigga," I said, "those were mine. You can have a
problem with me.

7
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:30,186
Leave the cook out of it." A guard behind her laughed once before
remembering where he stood. Salma looked at me. Really looked. At the
bruised shoulder beneath my torn shirt, the badge, the sword at my
hip, my wife's hand resting against my arm. Maybe she expected a
monster to arrive more neatly separated from the people who loved him.

8
00:02:30,436 --> 00:02:53,828
Then the doors behind her locked. A heavy bolt slammed into place. She
turned. The guards looked at one another. Above us, a balcony door
opened. A palace officer stepped out with two Black Mantle men.
"Captain Salma Vale," he called. "Your loyalty is under review." Noor
drew her gun. "Salma, move!" The officer fired.

9
00:02:54,078 --> 00:03:15,632
I hit Salma around the waist and drove her behind a marble bench as
the shot struck the place her head had occupied. Noor fired upward.
Shawna pulled Vesper into cover. Tank and Anton moved in front of the
younger guards, forcing them away from the open steps. Salma lay
beneath me for one second, staring at the balcony.

10
00:03:15,882 --> 00:03:37,273
"He ordered me to hold this door." "Nigga, he just updated the
assignment," I said. I got off her and fired at the balcony rail. The
officer ducked. Noor reached her sister and pulled her close, one hand
behind her head like she had done it a thousand times before either
woman owned a gun. "You hit?" Salma shook her head.

11
00:03:37,523 --> 00:04:01,492
"No." "Then think while you're alive." The younger woman swallowed.
Then she turned toward her guards. "Cover the stairs!" They obeyed
her. Not Noor. Not me. Their own captain, choosing where the next
bullet ought to go. Nigga, I respected that so much I almost forgot
the door remained a problem. Almost. "Tank!" He looked at the locked
doors. Then at me.

12
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:27,302
"You want the quiet opening or the brother opening?" "Nigga, read the
room." He grinned and called Anton. The two giants hit the doors
together. Marble dust fell from the frame. They hit them again. One of
Salma's guards stared. "Those men—" "Are on the guest list," Shawna
said. The third impact broke the lower hinge. Tank grabbed the edge.
Anton caught the other side.

13
00:04:27,552 --> 00:04:49,962
Together they dragged the door inward with a scream of metal that
sounded like the palace reconsidering its construction standards. I
went through first. The hall beyond was empty. Too empty. Mirrors
reflected us from every wall. Gold lamps shone above a long carpet. At
the far end, a staircase rose to another set of doors.

14
00:04:50,212 --> 00:05:14,086
On the carpet between stood a single black grand piano. I stopped.
"Baby." "I see it." A sheet of paper rested on the piano. FOR MRS.
AIDEN. AN ENCORE. Shawna looked at the note and shook her head. "Nigga
keeps booking shows without checking my calendar." A curtain moved
above us. I saw the gun behind it. "Down!" The mirrors shattered.

15
00:05:14,336 --> 00:05:38,345
Gunfire ripped across the hall from the upper galleries. Glass burst
into a thousand glittering pieces. Tank kicked the piano sideways,
turning it into cover. We dropped behind it while Noor and Salma
pulled their guards through the damaged doorway. Nigga, I had entered
enough expensive rooms lately that I was beginning to understand why
rich people insured things.

16
00:05:38,595 --> 00:05:59,138
Shawna crouched beside me, her back against the piano. "You think he
has a second song request?" "Yeah. It's called Stop Shooting My
Fucking Furniture." She laughed, then rose just enough to fire toward
the nearest gallery. I moved with her. Tank and Anton took the left
staircase. Noor and Salma took the right.

17
00:05:59,388 --> 00:06:21,428
Vesper stayed with the guards at the door, reading the room through
the remaining mirrors, calling where she saw movement. "Above the red
curtain!" I fired. A gun fell from the gallery and struck the marble.
"Behind the clock!" Shawna's shot shattered the clock face. The guard
behind it vanished backward with a shout. The women did not miss much.

18
00:06:21,678 --> 00:06:39,004
I reached the central stairs as a Black Mantle fighter came down
toward me. He swung a heavy pistol like a hammer. I caught his wrist,
hit his elbow, and drove him against the railing. The gun went over.
He came after it until I caught the back of his coat.

19
00:06:39,254 --> 00:07:01,466
For one second the nigga hung above the hall, his life attached to the
hand of the man he had tried to kill. "You done?" I asked. He nodded
frantically. "Use words." "I'm done!" I pulled him back over and put
him on the floor. "Excellent progress." Another man appeared above me
with a long blade. I drew Knox's sword. The nigga stopped.

20
00:07:01,716 --> 00:07:24,558
"Oh," he said. "Yeah," I replied. "They gave me one too." He attacked.
Steel rang across the staircase. I blocked, stepped back, and felt the
old bruise in my shoulder send a complaint directly to my brain. The
man was quick. He knew the stairs. He kept pressing me toward the
broken railing. I let him think it was working.

21
00:07:24,808 --> 00:07:46,738
Then I stepped onto the narrow ledge beside the stairs, caught the
hanging lamp chain with my free hand, and swung around his back.
Nigga, the look on his face when I landed above him belonged in a
museum. I struck his blade aside and drove the sword's hilt into his
chest. He lost his footing and sat down hard on the steps.

22
00:07:46,988 --> 00:08:11,367
Before he could rise, Shawna stood below him with her pistol raised.
"Stay seated," she said. The nigga stayed seated. I looked down at
her. "Teamwork." "Your shoulder." "Complaining." "I am going to join
it." We reached the upper landing together. Below us, the hall's
gunfire stopped one burst at a time. Tank came out of the left gallery
dragging a guard by the belt.

23
00:08:11,618 --> 00:08:31,939
Anton carried two more by the backs of their coats. Noor and Salma
stood on the right with their weapons raised over a row of
surrendering men. The younger captain looked across the hall at her
sister. For a moment both women were too far apart to touch. Then Noor
smiled. Salma smiled back.

24
00:08:32,189 --> 00:08:49,720
Nigga, there was a whole childhood in that look, and no emperor owned
a minute of it. A palace phone rang on a side table. Everybody froze.
I walked over and answered. "Captain Aiden's extremely busy
afternoon." Zero's voice filled my ear.

25
00:08:49,969 --> 00:09:13,985
"You have destroyed a room built by kings." I looked at the broken
mirrors, the shattered clock, the piano Tank had used as a barricade.
"Nigga, send the kings my apologies." "You think destruction proves
greatness." "No. You shooting your own captain proved something,
though." Silence. Then the emperor spoke more quietly. "Come to the
midnight court. Bring the crown.

26
00:09:14,235 --> 00:09:36,248
Let us settle what you came for." "You finally meeting me without
shooting through a curtain?" "The court will witness us." I looked at
Vesper below. She heard enough from my face to understand. "What
court?" I asked. "The rulers you have impressed. The captains you have
stolen. The people who believe you can offer them something I cannot.

27
00:09:36,498 --> 00:09:58,739
I have invited them to see you closely." "Nigga, they'll need better
chairs. My people travel heavy." He disconnected. I set down the
phone. Shawna came to my side. "He wants an audience." "So do I."
"Aiden." I turned toward her. She touched my bruised shoulder, then
the cross beneath my shirt. "Finish it." No flourish.

28
00:09:58,989 --> 00:10:17,957
No speech about what kind of man I ought to become after the shooting
stopped. Just my wife asking for the thing we had both carried across
every road that brought us here. I kissed her. "I will." Down in the
hall, Salma finally called her mother. Noor stood beside her while the
phone rang.

29
00:10:18,207 --> 00:10:32,264
When the older woman's voice answered, both captains closed their
eyes. I looked away and let them have it. Then I called Marcellus.
"Bring the crown," I said. "That nigga wants to see how it looks on
me."
